          "snippet": {
            "text": "/--\nFor `1 < re s` the L-function of a Dirichlet character agrees with the sum of the naive Dirichlet\nseries.\n-/\nlemma LFunction_eq_LSeries (χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ N) {s : ℂ} (hs : 1 < re s) :\n    LFunction χ s = LSeries (χ ·) s :=\n  ZMod.LFunction_eq_LSeries χ hs",
            "line": 70,
            "truncated": false
          },
          "proof_context": {
            "declaration": "DirichletCharacter.LFunction_eq_LSeries",
            "lines": [
              70,
              76
            ],
            "conclusion": "For `1 < Re s`, the analytically continued `χ.LFunction s` equals `LSeries (χ ·) s`, i.e. `L(s,χ) = Σ χ(n) n^{-s}`."
          },
